! The `ph.x` input that generated `reference.out.ph-bismuthene-epsilon-us-soc`,
! so that the reference is regenerable rather than merely committed.
!
!   pw.x -in bismuthene-epsilon-us-soc.in && ph.x -in bismuthene-epsilon-us-soc.ph.in
!
! with `outdir` pointing at the same scratch for both. The dielectric constant is
! what `epsil = .true.` prints at the end. (fully-relativistic ultrasoft
! bismuthene, the heavy-element case.)
dielectric constant of bismuthene, ultrasoft, spin-orbit
 &inputph
  tr2_ph = 1.0d-14,
  epsil = .true.,
  fildyn = 'bi.dynG',
  amass(1) = 208.98,
 /
0.0 0.0 0.0
